      <!-- 1 -->
      <section id="introduction">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>

        <p>
          Welcome to <strong>Omni Notes</strong>. Omni Notes is a
          note-taking and productivity application designed to help
          users create, organize, manage, and access their personal
          notes and related content.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information may be processed
          when you use Omni Notes and how that information may be handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          For the purposes of this Privacy Policy, "Omni Notes",
          "we", "us", or "our" refers to the developer or publisher
          responsible for the application.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 2 -->
      <section id="information">
        <h2>Information We May Collect</h2>

        <p>
          Depending on the features you use, Omni Notes may process
          different categories of information.
        </p>

        <h3>Information You Provide</h3>

        <ul>
          <li>Notes, text, titles, checklists, and other content you create.</li>
          <li>Images or photographs that you choose to attach to notes.</li>
          <li>Voice recordings or audio content that you choose to create.</li>
          <li>Folders, categories, tags, colors, and other organizational data.</li>
          <li>Account information if account-based features are enabled.</li>
          <li>Information you provide when contacting our support team.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Device and Technical Information</h3>

        <p>
          Depending on the services and permissions enabled in the app,
          certain technical information may be processed, such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Device model and operating system version.</li>
          <li>Application version.</li>
          <li>Basic diagnostic or crash information.</li>
          <li>General app interaction information.</li>
          <li>IP address or approximate location information where required by certain third-party services.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Omni Notes does not intentionally request sensitive personal
          information unless it is necessary for a specific feature and
          you voluntarily provide it.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 3 -->
      <section id="notes">
        <h2>Your Notes and Content</h2>

        <p>
          The content you create inside Omni Notes may include personal
          information because notes are created by you.
        </p>

        <p>
          This may include text, tasks, checklists, images, audio
          recordings, drawings, tags, folders, and other content depending
          on the features available in the application.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Your content belongs to you.</strong>
          You are responsible for the information you choose to store
          inside your notes and for ensuring that your notes do not contain
          information that you do not have permission to store or share.
        </div>

        <p>
          If Omni Notes provides cloud synchronization or account-based
          backup, your selected content may be transmitted to the relevant
          backend service so that synchronization and backup features can
          operate.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 4 -->
      <section id="permissions">
        <h2>App Permissions</h2>

        <p>
          Omni Notes may request certain Android permissions when required
          for features you choose to use.
        </p>

        <div class="info-grid">

          <div class="info-card">
            <strong>Photos / Media</strong>
            Used when you choose to select or attach images or media
            to your notes.
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <strong>Microphone</strong>
            Used only when you choose to create or record voice notes.
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <strong>Notifications</strong>
            May be used for reminders, updates, or other notification
            features if enabled.
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <strong>Internet</strong>
            May be required for synchronization, updates, analytics,
            advertisements, or other online features.
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          You can manage supported permissions through your Android
          device settings. Disabling a permission may prevent the
          corresponding feature from working correctly.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 5 -->
      <section id="usage">
        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>

        <p>
          Information processed through Omni Notes may be used for the
          following purposes:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>To provide and operate the application's features.</li>
          <li>To save and display your notes and content.</li>
          <li>To provide synchronization or backup features where available.</li>
          <li>To provide reminders and notifications when enabled.</li>
          <li>To improve application performance and reliability.</li>
          <li>To diagnose crashes, bugs, and technical problems.</li>
          <li>To protect the application against abuse or unauthorized activity.</li>
          <li>To provide customer support.</li>
          <li>To display advertisements if advertising is enabled.</li>
          <li>To understand general application usage and improve the user experience.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>


      <!-- 6 -->
      <section id="storage">
        <h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>

        <p>
          Omni Notes may store information locally on your device and,
          where applicable, on secure servers or third-party infrastructure
          used to provide online features.
        </p>

        <p>
          We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to
          protect information from unauthorized access, alteration,
          disclosure, or destruction.
        </p>

        <p>
          However, no electronic storage system, internet transmission,
          or application can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
          Therefore, we cannot guarantee absolute security of your data.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Backup recommendation:</strong>
          If Omni Notes provides export or backup functionality, we
          recommend maintaining your own backup of important notes and
          personal content.
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- 7 -->
      <section id="thirdparty">
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

        <p>
          Omni Notes may use third-party services to provide certain
          functionality, including hosting, authentication, cloud storage,
          analytics, crash reporting, notifications, or advertising.
        </p>

        <p>
          These third-party providers may process certain information
          according to their own privacy policies and terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          Examples of third-party services that may be used include
          Google Play Services, Firebase, Google Analytics for Firebase,
          Firebase Crashlytics, Google AdMob, or other services required
          by the application.
        </p>

        <p>
          Only services actually integrated into the released version of
          Omni Notes should be considered applicable.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 8 -->
      <section id="ads">
        <h2>Advertising</h2>

        <p>
          If advertising is enabled in Omni Notes, advertisements may be
          provided by third-party advertising providers such as Google
          AdMob.
        </p>

        <p>
          Advertising providers may process information such as advertising
          identifiers, device information, approximate location, and
          interaction information in accordance with their own policies.
        </p>

        <p>
          Advertising practices may vary depending on your device,
          region, consent choices, and the advertising configuration
          used by the application.
        </p>

        <p>
          If Omni Notes does not display advertisements in the version
          you are using, this section does not apply to your use of those
          advertising features.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 9 -->
      <section id="analytics">
        <h2>Analytics</h2>

        <p>
          Omni Notes may use analytics or diagnostic tools to understand
          application performance and improve the user experience.
        </p>

        <p>
          Such information may include general usage events, application
          version, device information, crash information, and performance
          data.
        </p>

        <p>
          Analytics information is intended to help us identify bugs,
          improve features, understand general usage patterns, and
          maintain application stability.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 10 -->
      <section id="sharing">
        <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information may be shared or processed only when reasonably
          necessary to operate Omni Notes, provide requested features,
          maintain technical infrastructure, comply with legal obligations,
          or protect the security and rights of users and the service.
        </p>

        <p>
          Third-party service providers may receive limited information
          necessary to perform services on our behalf.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 11 -->
      <section id="retention">
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>

        <p>
          Information may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary
          to provide the requested services, maintain application
          functionality, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes,
          enforce agreements, and maintain security.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information stored locally on your device generally remains
          there until you delete it, clear the application data, uninstall
          the application, or otherwise remove it through available
          application features.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 12 -->
      <section id="deletion">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>

        <p>
          You may delete notes and other content using the available
          features inside Omni Notes.
        </p>

        <p>
          If Omni Notes provides an account or cloud-based service,
          you may request deletion of your account and associated data
          by contacting us.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some information may need to be retained where required by law,
          for legitimate security purposes, or where necessary to resolve
          disputes and prevent abuse.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Data deletion request:</strong>
          Contact us using the email address provided at the bottom of
          this Privacy Policy and include enough information for us to
          identify your request.
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- 13 -->
      <section id="children">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          Omni Notes is not intended to knowingly collect personal
          information from children in violation of applicable laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you believe that a child has provided personal information
          through the application without appropriate consent, please
          contact us so that we can review and take appropriate action.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 14 -->
      <section id="security">
        <h2>Security</h2>

        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect information handled by
          Omni Notes. However, you should understand that no method of
          electronic transmission or storage is completely secure.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are also responsible for protecting access to your device,
          account credentials, and any backup or synchronization account
          connected to Omni Notes.
        </p>
      </section>


      <!-- 15 -->
      <section id="changes">
        <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
          changes in the application, technology, legal requirements,
          or our practices.
        </p>

        <p>
          When changes are made, the updated policy will be published on
          this page and the "Last Updated" date will be changed accordingly.
        </p>

        <p>
          We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
        </p>
      </section>


